it. The check exits 1 only on drift: a broken or foreign link, including a broken link inside a merged folder, a missing source or a tracked absolute link. Missing children in a partial merge do not count as drift. Add `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\\n\\n| Status | What it means for this install |\\n|--------|-------------------------------|\\n| `linked-whole` | Already a link into the checkout. Step 1 has nothing to do for it |\\n| `linked-merge` | A real folder whose children are links. Nothing to do |\\n| `partial-merge` | A real folder missing some links. Step 1 fills the gaps and never deletes a local file |\\n| `missing` | Not there yet. Step 1 creates it |\\n| `broken` | A link whose target is gone. Step 1 replaces it |\\n| `foreign-link` | A link that points somewhere else. Left alone, and the engine refuses to touch it |\\n| `local` | A real file or folder of the repo\\'s own. Left alone |\\n| `source-missing` | The checkout has no such path. Nothing is planned |\\n\\n## 6. The Ordered Steps\\n\\nThis is the checklist, and it is also what `list`, `?` and `menu` print. Each step carries its exact command, its class and one line of why.\\n\\nThe class column is the manifest\\'s `mutating` value for the route that owns the printed command, verbatim, so it is read from the route table and never guessed. A command with no route of its own prints `n/a`.\\n\\n```text\\n1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>   [class]\\n   Why: creates the links. It shows a plan first and asks before it writes.\\n\\n2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>   [class]\\n   Why: keeps the repo\\'s own AGENTS.md and refreshes the shipped sections into it. Dropped when the instruction choice is link.\\n\\n3) /doctor:mcp install   [class]\\n   Why: builds and registers Code Mode. Run it from the Skilled checkout.\\n\\n4) /doctor:git setup   [class]\\n   Why: checks the git hooks and sk-git settings, and names the repair for each